    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d171">

                <pb facs="0402" n="370" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v18/pg370"/>

                <head>171. Telegram From the Department of State to the Embassy in Israel<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d171-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1965-03-01T12:16:00-05:00">March 1, 1965, 12:16 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <p>848. Eyes only for Harriman from Secretary. Tel Aviv’s 1075.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d171-f2"/> Please believe me my telegram 847 was not intended to
                    reflect slightest doubt regarding clarity, vigor and force with which you have
                    presented our views during these past four difficult days. On contrary, we can
                    see from your reporting that you have stood very firm against powerful
                    onslaught.</p>
                <p>Forceful reiteration in my telegram of points already essentially covered in your
                    initial instructions was intended simply to give you renewed authority to press
                    Israelis to utmost. It reflected continuing and growing feeling by the President
                    that there are limits beyond which we cannot go in support of Israel. He wanted
                    you to be sure that even the strong case which Eshkol has made on Israel’s
                    behalf could not be <pb facs="0403" n="371" xml:id="pg371"/> allowed to override
                    what he considers to be basic interest of US. If we cannot pursue a policy which
                    enables us to further our overall interests in the Middle East, he would prefer
                    to shift responsibility for that area’s stability to other hands.</p>
                <p>I think you have done splendid job, regardless of how your final session today
                    comes out, and you have my warmest and most sincere thanks. Good luck and happy
                    landings for the rest of your trip.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold"> Rusk </hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
